<div class="expl-card concept-card"><div class="section-title-concept">📌 Core Concept: IPv6 Well-Known Multicast Addresses</div><p>IPv6 has no broadcast.</p><p>Instead, devices use well-known link-local multicast addresses in the FF02 range.</p><p>Each address reaches one specific group.</p></div>
  <div class="expl-card correct-card"><h4 class="section-title-correct">✓ Why the Correct Answer (Option C) is Correct:</h4><ul><li><span class="opt-tag correct">Option C</span> <strong>FF02::6</strong>: <strong>FF02::6</strong> is the well-known multicast address reserved for <strong>All OSPF DRs/BDRs</strong>.</li></ul></div>
  <div class="expl-card incorrect-card"><h4 class="section-title-incorrect">✗ Why Other Options are Incorrect:</h4><ul><li><span class="opt-tag wrong">Option A</span> <strong>FF02::2</strong>: This address belongs to the <strong>All routers</strong> group, not All OSPF DRs/BDRs.</li><li><span class="opt-tag wrong">Option B</span> <strong>FF02::9</strong>: This address belongs to the <strong>All RIP routers</strong> group, not All OSPF DRs/BDRs.</li><li><span class="opt-tag wrong">Option D</span> <strong>FF02::5</strong>: This address belongs to the <strong>All OSPF routers</strong> group, not All OSPF DRs/BDRs.</li></ul></div>
